<!-- optimised -->

    This is the heapify method. The approach is:
    compare the node with its left and right child,
    find the largest among them, and swap if needed.

    While building the heap, we skip all leaf nodes
    because leaf nodes already satisfy the heap property.

    we run loop from nonleaf to 0 th index 

    In a complete binary tree, about half the nodes are leaves.
    As we move upward, the number of nodes decreases while
    the cost of heapify increases.

    bottom level  n/2 nodes    cost is 0 (because it satifies the heap condition so we skip them)
    above         n/4 nodes     cost is 1 
    .
    .
    .

    for only level first we have cost of logn 

    so we can't just add up all the cost 

    TC: O(n)
    SC: O(log n)   // due to recursive heapify call stack